Let $G$ be a countable group. For each $j\in\N$, let $k_j$ be a positive integer, put \[ \mathcal H_j=\ell^2(G;\C^{k_j}), \qquad (U_j(g)\xi)(x)=\xi(g^{-1}x), \] and let $A_j,T_j\in\mathcal B(\mathcal H_j)$ with $A_j\in U_j(G)'$. Write \[ A_j[x,y]=W_j(x^{-1}y),\qquad E_j=\sum_{s\in G}
orm{W_j(s)}_{\HS}^2. \] Suppose that one constant $K\ge0$ satisfies  egin{align*} 
orm{\operatorname{row}_e(T_j)}&\le K, & 
orm{\operatorname{col}_e(A_j-T_j)}&\le K &&(j\in\N),\ 
orm{T_j-U_j(g)T_jU_j(g)^{-1}}&\le K &&&&(j\in\N,\ g\in G). \end{align*} Assume also that \[  rac{E_j}{k_j}\longrightarrow\infty. \] Then $G$ has a representation on a separable complex Hilbert space whose operators are bounded and invertible, with \[ \sup_{g\in G}
orm{\pi(g)}\le1+K, \] and which is not similar to a unitary representation. No uniform bound on $
orm{T_j}$ or $
orm{A_j}$ is assumed.
